            <ArticleTitle>Intravenous xenon- 133 for the determination of radionuclide first pass right ventricular ejection fraction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>626-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The use of intravenous xenon- 133 for determination of radionuclide first pass right ventricular ejection fraction is described. First pass determinations of right ventricular ejection fraction were made with both xenon- 133 and technetium-99m in 13 subjects (15 right ventricular ejection fraction determinations); results obtained with xenon- 133 show an excellent correlation (r = 0.98, p less than 0.002) with results obtained using technetium-99m. Because of rapid pulmonary elimination of xenon- 133 from the body, the use of this radioisotope allows multiple first pass right ventricular ejection fraction determinations within a short period of time, without significant radiation exposure for the patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
